{
  "summary": "Removes the `manual_connection` boolean flag from `ConnectDirectly()` and `ConnectToSocket()`, returning an `util::Expected<std::unique_ptr<Sock>, std::string>` with the failure reason to callers instead of logging directly inside the connection helpers. Callers in `net.cpp`, `torcontrol.cpp`, `Proxy::Connect()`, and `bitcoin-cli.cpp` are updated to handle the expected result and determine their own logging behavior.",
  "problem": "`ConnectDirectly()` logs connection failures internally and only uses the `manual_connection` flag to decide between info and debug log levels. Non-manual callers like Tor control are forced to pass `manual_connection=true` just to ensure failures are logged, while none of the callers can inspect or customize the failure error string.",
  "evidence": [
    "PR description: 'Callers that are not manual peers, like Tor control, pass `true` just to get the failure logged, and the caller that knows how much a failure matters never sees the reason.'"
  ],
  "dependencies": {
    "depends_on": [
      "#36969"
    ],
    "enables": []
  },
  "scope_notes": "The PR is stacked on #36969; the first two commits and their tests belong to #36969, while only the final commit (`netbase: Return the reason for a failed connection instead of logging it`) is new to this PR.",
  "changed_since_previous": "The diff and commits were previously unavailable (patch-id nopatch); full commit history and patch details are now provided.",
  "card": "This draft PR removes the manual_connection parameter from ConnectDirectly(), returning failure error strings via util::Expected so callers can decide their own logging policies. Currently, callers like Tor control pass manual_connection=true solely to trigger failure logging, without access to the underlying error details. The change updates callers across net, torcontrol, and proxy handling to log failures contextually. It depends on base PR #36969.",
